---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// DRAFT — "Before a flood" guided path. Wayfinding only; links into cited pages.
// Step content traced to the coalition workflows running notes (Path 1). No
// toolkit field content restated.
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Before a flood | Workflows | Resilience Hub Toolkit"
  description="Getting organized before a flood: a guided path that helps your community build the roles, relationships, and contacts you will rely on when water rises."
>
  <section class="py-12">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 max-w-3xl">
      <nav class="text-body-small text-muted-foreground mb-6" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/workflows" class="hover:text-primary underline underline-offset-2">Workflows</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> / </span>
        <span class="text-foreground">Before a flood</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-hero font-semibold mb-4 text-foreground">Before a flood</h1>
      <p class="text-body-large text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-3">
        Getting organized before a disaster. These are the moves that build the
        roles, relationships, and contacts your community will lean on when water
        rises. Start wherever fits where you already are.
      </p>

      <!-- Navigation video slot (coming later) -->
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-dashed border-primary/40 bg-muted p-5 my-8">
        <p class="text-label uppercase-accent text-primary mb-1">Walkthrough video, coming soon</p>
        <p class="text-body-small text-muted-foreground">
          A short video will walk through this path. It is not recorded yet.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="space-y-6 list-none">
        <li>
          <h2 class="text-subtitle font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">1. Gather a group of people together</h2>
          <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground">
            A handful of neighbors who are willing to organize is enough to begin.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2 class="text-subtitle font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">2. Choose a structure that works for your group</h2>
          <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground">
            Keep it as simple as the people you have can sustain.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2 class="text-subtitle font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">3. Decide on roles that fit the people you have</h2>
          <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground mb-2">
            Figure out what each person can reliably offer: volunteer coordination,
            shelter support, animal care, child care, meals. Roles to consider:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 text-body text-muted-foreground">
            <li>Lead organizer</li>
            <li>Volunteer coordinator</li>
            <li>Data coordinator</li>
            <li>Response / tool coordinator</li>
            <li>Outreach coordinator</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-dashed border-border bg-muted p-4 mt-3">
            <p class="text-body-small text-muted-foreground">
              <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Placeholder for the team:</span>
              the running notes point to a tool that helps a group figure out roles.
              We will link it here once the team confirms which one.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <h2 class="text-subtitle font-semibold text-foreground mb-1">4. Meet your Emergency Management Director (EMD)</h2>
          <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground mb-2">
            Find your EMD through your town clerk. Ask how they want to be reached on
            day one of an emergency, and who else they want you to contact. Add their
            contact to the
            <a href="/modules/emergency-preparedness/1-9#leader-directory" class="text-primary underline underline-offset-2">Directory of Local Leaders</a>.
          </p>
          <div class="rounded-lg border border-dashed border-border bg-muted p-4 mt-3">
            <p class="text-body-small text-muted-foreground">
              <span class="text-foreground font-medium">Placeholder for the team:</span>
              if your area needs a regional list rather than a local one, the team is
              working out a shared regional template. Coming soon.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted p-5 mt-10">
        <p class="text-body text-muted-foreground">
          This path is the digital companion to the in-person
          <span class="text-foreground">muck-and-gut workshop</span>, which opens with
          getting organized before a disaster. The workshop and these workflows are
          built to fit together.
        </p>
      </div>

      <nav class="flex items-center justify-between border-t border-border mt-10 pt-6 text-body-small" aria-label="Path navigation">
        <a href="/workflows" class="text-muted-foreground hover:text-primary underline underline-offset-2">All workflows</a>
        <a href="/workflows/response" class="text-primary font-medium underline underline-offset-2">Next: Responding to a flood &rarr;</a>
      </nav>

      <p class="text-body-small text-muted-foreground mt-8">
        Shaped by the Resilience Hub Toolkit coalition, with RAFT VT, NEK Organizing,
        and CROs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
